{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "duo_lmars_ustar_a",
    "description": "LMARS interface normal velocity u* = 1/2(uE + uW) + (piE - piW)/(2 a) (Chen 2021 Eq 13), with the acoustic wave speed a supplied EXPLICITLY as a parameter rather than recomputed from (piE,piW). This matches the reference code default in which a is formed from the two adjacent CELL pressures (a = duo_lmars_a(dp_L, dp_R)) while the pressure jump piE-piW uses the face-reconstructed pressures -- the two use different pressure pairs, so the speed cannot be recovered from (piE,piW) alone (contrast duo_lmars_ustar, which bundles a = duo_lmars_a(piE,piW)). AXIS-NEUTRAL scalar algebra.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:duo",
      "op:riemann",
      "scheme:lmars"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Chen, X. (2021). The LMARS based shallow-water dynamical core on generic gnomonic cubed-sphere geometry. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 13(1), e2020MS002280.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2020MS002280"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "duo_lmars_ustar_a": {
      "params": [
        "uE",
        "uW",
        "piE",
        "piW",
        "a"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              0.5,
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "uE",
                  "uW"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "piE",
                  "piW"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  2,
                  "a"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}